 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication and roles
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on every request. A missing or unknown
+key returns `401 unauthorized`. A key without the required role returns
+`403 forbidden`.
+
+- `viewer` can use all GET routes except `/audit`.
+- `cook` can also use `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures`, and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` can use every route.
+
+`GET /audit` returns a manager-only array sorted newest first. Each request
+that changes data records `at` (a UTC timestamp), `keyName`, `method`, `path`
+(the URL pathname), and `status` (the HTTP response code).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
